Other interactions:
* {{I|8 Inch Nails}}: Beams gain knockback, pushing enemies away in the direction they travel but not out of their path. This increases its consistency.
* {{I|Abyss}}: When Isaac uses Abyss to absorb Brimstone, it turns into a larger gray locust, but otherwise acts like normal locusts created by Abyss.
* {{I|Bird's Eye}}: Will occasionally spawn a fire when firing.
* {{I|Chocolate Milk|dlc=nr}}: Reduces Isaac's tear delay by 20%. Does not increase damage.
* {{I|Dr. Fetus|nar}}: Overrides Brimstone.
** {{dlc|anr}} Isaac continuously fires bombs while charging the beam.
* {{I|Epic Fetus|na}}: Overrides Brimstone.
* {{I|Epiphora}}: Effect only activates when holding charge in a specific direction, and deactivates when the charge is released, effectively making Epiphora useless unless Isaac has exceedingly high tear delay.
* {{I|Fire Mind}}: The beam will not cause explosions, but will still set enemies on [[burn|fire]].
* {{C|The Forgotten|a+}}: The charged attack will spawn a Brimstone ball that will float in front of The Forgotten for a few seconds before disappearing. The Forgotten will still melee attack while performing this action.
* {{I|Ghost Pepper|a+nr}}: The flames can still shoot from Isaac while holding the fire button.
** {{Dlc|r}} Has a chance to shoot flames for every other tick while the beam is being fired.
* {{I|Godhead}}: Homing and stat bonuses apply, but the beam does not have a damaging aura.
* {{I|Ipecac|na+}}: Does not apply Ipecac's stat changes. The beam poisons enemies.
** {{Dlc|a+nr}}Isaac shoots Ipecac tears while charging Brimstone. Stat changes from both items are applied as normal, meaning that Ipecac fires slower and Brimstone charges slower, but Brimstone deals drastically increased damage.
** {{Dlc+|r}}Applies +2 flat damage, instead of Ipecac's damage up. Does not apply Ipecac's tears down. The beam explodes on the first enemy or obstacle it hits every other tick, dealing 10 + twice of Isaac's Damage. The beam gains a poison effect. The explosions do not occur when the beam narrows, meaning that they occur only twice per shot without {{I|Soy Milk}} / {{I|Almond Milk}}. The beam and its explosions poison enemies. {{I|The Ladder}}, when placed, will trigger the Ipecac-Brimstone explosions. (possibly a bug)
*** '''Ipecac''' + {{I|Haemolacria}}: The flat damage bonus is +40 instead of +2. Tears will explode into multiple brimstone beams, each of which explodes and has a chance to hit Isaac.{{dlc-}}
* {{I|Isaac's Tears|na+}}: Fires normal tears, but nearly instantly charges when charging Brimstone.
** {{dlc|a+nr}}Fires normal tears. Charges at the same rate as Isaac's fire rate while charging Brimstone.
** {{dlc|r}}Fires normal tears. Charges when firing Brimstone.
* {{I|Knockout Drops}}: Gives the lasers high knockback.
* {{I|Lachryphagy|r}}: Brimstone's range is lowered, but Lachryphagy tears will form at the end of the beam, which can be fed.
* {{I|Large Zit}}: Creep shots will still be fired occasionally while holding the fire button.
* {{I|Lodestone}}: Changes the beam to gray, can still apply the magnetized effect. The beams are not attracted to enemies with the magnetized effect.
* {{I|Number One}}: Although Number One is otherwise purely beneficial with standard Brimstone, {{C|Azazel}}'s range is severely affected.
* {{I|Playdough Cookie}}: Brimstone will start cycling through colors and applies the standard chance of tear-effect on hit, with the homing effect occurring intermittently.
* {{I|Pop!|r}}: Brimstone has shorter range, a bit longer than the default range of {{C|Azazel}}'s mini-Brimstone, and it is not affected by [[range]]. The beam fires Pop! tears at the end, which are [[piercing]].
* {{I|Proptosis|na}}: Does not apply distance penalty.
** {{Dlc|anr}}The beam deals 2× Isaac's Damage, which is already doubled from the item's effect, at point blank-range. The damage quickly drops further along the beam, at about 0.8× per tile of distance.
** {{Dlc|r}}The beam deals 6× Isaac's Damage at point-blank range. Decreases 13.3% of the damage per tile of distance, to the minimum of 0.1 point of damage at 7.5 tiles of distance.
* {{I|Spirit Sword}}: Overrides Brimstone.
* {{C|Tainted Samson|r}}: Greatly decreases attack speed for Samson's rage mode melee attack and replaces the thrown jawbone with a large laser sphere (similarly to {{C|The Forgotten}}).

