sections.Interactions:
* Following items leave the creep pools:
** {{I|Eye of Greed}}
** {{I|Fate's Reward}}
** {{T|Found Soul}}
** {{I|Gello}}
** {{I|Host Hat}}
** {{I|Incubus}}
** {{I|Kidney Stone}}
** {{I|Lead Pencil}}
** {{I|Metal Plate}}
** {{I|Sad Bombs}}
** {{I|Saturnus}}
** {{I|Tammy's Head}}
** {{I|Twisted Pair}}
** {{I|Varicose Veins}}
* Following items do not leave the creep pools:
** {{I|Akeldama}}
** {{I|Brimstone Bombs}}
** {{I|Circle of Protection}}
** {{I|Divine Intervention}}
** {{I|It Hurts}}
** {{I|Large Zit}}
** {{I|Shard of Glass}}
** {{I|Slipped Rib}}
** {{I|Vasculitis}}
* {{I|Athame}} / {{I|Maw Of The Void}}: Only creates the creep pools when damaging enemies or destroyable obstacles.
* {{I|Brimstone}}: Overrides Mysterious Liquid.
** {{Dlc|a}} The beam spawns pools of liquid always when it hits obstacles and enemies on a constant time interval.
*** {{C|Azazel}}: Leaves the creep pools at the end of Azazel's shorter brimstone beam.
* {{I|Dr. Fetus}} / {{I|Epic Fetus}} / {{I|Ipecac}}: Overrides Mysterious Liquid.
** {{Dlc|a}} Explosions caused by these items will leave a large pool of creep.
* {{I|Fire Mind}}: Mysterious Liquid removes explosion chance, but fire damage over time is preserved.
** {{Dlc|a}} Tears can explode as expected. The explosions leave a large pool of creep.
* {{I|Haemolacria}}: Only the main tear spawns creep.
** {{Dlc|r}} All tears leave the creep pools .
* {{I|Lachryphagy}}: Only the burst tears spawns creep.
* {{I|Lost Contact}}: Overrides Mysterious Liquid.
** {{Dlc|a+}} The combination works as expected, with tears spawning liquid even when stopping enemy shots.
* {{I|The Ludovico Technique}}: Mysterious Liquid's graphical effect remains, but the tear leaves no creep.
** {{Dlc|a}} The tear leaves a trail of creep pools on a constant time interval.
* {{I|Montezuma's Revenge}}: Constantly creates pools of creep at the end of the beam. Corn projectiles do not spawn creep.
* {{I|Mucormycosis}}: All tears including spores spawn creep upon burst, but not on contact with enemies.
* {{t|Nose Goblin}} / {{I|Sinus Infection}}: Spawns creep after each tear's effect wears off and drops to the ground but not on contact with enemies.
* [[Piercing tears]]: Tears do not leave creep pools  when they hit and pass through an enemy, and only leave creep pools when they hit an obstacle or run out of range.
* {{I|Revelation}}: The beam spawns pools of liquid always when it hits obstacles and enemies on a constant time interval.
* {{I|Rubber Cement}}: Tears do not create creep when they bounce off enemies or obstacles and only when they land.
* [[Spectral tears]]: Tears only spawn creep pools after they land, not while passing through obstacles.
* {{I|Strange Attractor}}: Overrides Mysterious Liquid.
** {{Dlc|a+}} The combination works as expected.
* {{I|Technology}}: Overrides Mysterious Liquid.
** {{Dlc|a}} The laser spawns pools of liquid always when it hits obstacles and occasionally on enemies.

